post-it: Computer smells weird and won't start
symptoms:
	Hangs and reboots at startup
		shows: a second into the Windows startup sound, the computer stops answering and the sound sags, then it freezes in a buzz, and a few seconds later it reboots
	Computer overheating
		shows: the fan is covered by a dead hamster
hardware steps:
	Remove the computer shell
	Take out the hamster, throw it in the trash
	Remount the shell
notes:
	Broken part: None. A hamster lies on the fan; the fan itself is fine. Take the hamster out to fix it.
	One exception on purpose: Hamster has the symptoms of Dust Overheat, and the player tells them apart by opening the computer.
